{"id": "EUVD-2026-103084", "enisaUuid": "db5bc44b-e11d-3036-9b3c-982fee23490a", "description": "Chaskiq through 2.0.3 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to make the server fetch arbitrary URLs via the url parameter of the /oembed endpoint. Attackers can target loopback, private, or cloud-metadata addresses through FetchLinkCardService, which follows redirects and skips TLS verification, to read internal page titles and descriptions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:13:57", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/chaskiq-unauthenticated-ssrf-oembed-url-upload", "https://github.com/chaskiq/chaskiq/blob/2.0.3/app/controllers/oembed_controller.rb#L8-L11", "https://github.com/chaskiq/chaskiq/blob/2.0.3/app/services/fetch_link_card_service.rb#L11-L40", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/chaskiq-through-2.0.3-unauthenticated-ssrf-via-oembed-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111662", "GHSA-938p-qgmw-f5v3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c5df5ec-5f0f-3ccd-b18a-7ade6759303a", "product": {"name": "Chaskiq", "vendor": {"name": "chaskiq"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f1491c05-5250-3153-afde-aaf05e6e280f", "vendor": {"name": "chaskiq"}}], "isExploited": false}